---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import BlogPostLayout from '../../components/BlogPostLayout.astro';
import { site, deliverySlabLine, maxDeliveryKm } from '../../lib/data';
import { abs, blogPostingJsonLd, breadcrumbJsonLd } from '../../lib/seo';
const headline = 'How Our Cloud Kitchen Orders Work | The Oven Vibe';
const description = 'What a cloud kitchen means at The Oven Vibe: takeaway, direct delivery, kitchen confirmation and group-order planning in Sundargarh.';
const path = '/blog/cloud-kitchen-future/';
const image = {url:abs('/static/images/og/blog_5.jpg'),width:1200,height:630,alt:'The Oven Vibe food photograph'};

---
<Layout title={headline} description={description} ogType="article" image={image} jsonLd={[blogPostingJsonLd({headline,description,path,image:image.url,datePublished:'2024-06-05',dateModified:'2026-10-17'}),breadcrumbJsonLd([{name:'Blog',path:'/blog/'},{name:headline,path}])]}>
 <BlogPostLayout line1='A KITCHEN,' lineGradient='READY TO ORDER.' subtitle='How takeaway and delivery work at The Oven Vibe.'>
  <picture><source type="image/avif" srcset="/static/images/blog_images/blog_5.avif"/><source type="image/webp" srcset="/static/images/blog_images/blog_5.webp"/><img src="/static/images/blog_images/blog_5.webp" alt="The Oven Vibe food photograph" class="blog-img" loading="lazy" width="1024" height="1024"/></picture>

  <p>A cloud kitchen prepares food for takeaway and delivery instead of serving it at dine-in tables. At The Oven Vibe in {site.business.address.locality}, that means a pure vegetarian, egg-free menu, collection from the kitchen or direct delivery within the published area.</p>
  <h2>What changes for you?</h2><p>You choose from the same published menu, but you need a collection or delivery plan. There is no dine-in seating. Use the written item details for sizes, ingredients and combo contents; our own team photographs the food, but a picture is not a full order specification.</p>
  <h2>From choosing food to a confirmed order</h2><ol><li>Browse the <a href="/menu/">menu</a> or <a href="/choose/">compare the dishes</a>.</li><li>Add the items and check the basket, extras and quantities.</li><li>Select pickup or delivery, the distance and time, then review the final quote.</li><li>Hand the order to the kitchen's WhatsApp chat and wait for acceptance. If advance payment applies, follow the kitchen's instructions.</li></ol>
  <h2>Where can the kitchen deliver?</h2><p>Our own delivery area extends to {maxDeliveryKm} km. Standard distance rates are {deliverySlabLine}. Beyond this area, check an available delivery platform at your address. The website does not guarantee another service's coverage.</p>
  <h2>What about an office lunch or birthday?</h2><p>Tell the kitchen the date, time, headcount, preferred dishes, dietary requirements and pickup or delivery details. Confirm the quantities and final quote. This is a planning process, not a claim about events we have completed or a fixed price per guest.</p>
  <h2>What this guide does not measure</h2><p>We have not published a comparative study of restaurant overheads, food freshness or local market growth. Our own service model is useful to explain without claiming it makes every cloud kitchen cheaper or better than every dine-in restaurant.</p>

  <p><a href="/choose/">Compare ingredients, serving sizes and combos</a>, <a href="/menu/">browse the full menu</a>, or <a href="/faq/">read the ordering answers</a>.</p>
 </BlogPostLayout>
</Layout>
